  "behaviour": [
    "States: draft -> sealed (paid) -> live (from the first opening) -> resting (term ended) -> erased 12 months (365 days) after resting began unless kept or woken. Delete from any state -> removed; restorable for 30 days, then erased.",
    "Term starts at openedAt: endsAt = openedAt + term (moment 7, keepsake 14, signature 30, premiere 60 days) (T-44).",
    "Wedding wishes count the term from the wedding date (endsAt = weddingDate 00:00 in timeZone + term); a Save the date lives until the day, then its term (T-45).",
    "A keep moves endsAt forward (live) or sets status live with endsAt = now + keep days (resting). Pass (while active), Now Showing (while public) and a Pro plan (wishes on a business page, while active) keep a wish live without a keep (T-16).",
    "Moment cannot be kept (T-02).",
    "Erase now removes the wish and its files for good within 24 hours (T-50). Before erasure after rest, both people are offered the wish as a video file (T-49).",
    "Every transition is made by the server (jobs or a verified request), recorded in WishTransition; the client never sets status.",
    "Pro client wishes use sealed, live, resting (T-43)."
  ],
  "truths": [
    "T-43",
    "T-44",
    "T-45",
    "T-48",
    "T-49",
    "T-50"
  ]
}